# NIKATRU — browser extension factory · root .gitattributes
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true. Without this file, the
# first clone on a second machine checks every text file out with CRLF endings.
# Nothing looks broken — the extensions still load, the simulations still pass —
# but every shipped file's bytes differ from the bytes that were audited, the
# packaging script produces an archive with a different hash from the one that
# was reviewed, and the "restore byte-identical, verify the hash" doctrine these
# tools are graded by is quietly false on that machine only.
#
# That is the failure shape this project keeps getting bitten by: a claim that
# stays green locally while being wrong somewhere nobody looked. One line
# prevents it.
#
# Extension/Full_Screen_Shot/ carries its own .gitattributes repeating the same
# `* text=auto eol=lf` line for its own subtree. Attributes resolve per PATTERN,
# not per file: the nested file wins only for the patterns it states, and this
# root file still governs that subtree for everything it does not state —
# including the *.webm, *.ps1 and *.cmd lines.
#
# The nested file also marks its binaries `-text` where this one uses `binary`.
# ⚠️ THE OLD EXPLANATION OF THAT DIFFERENCE WAS BACKWARDS AND IS WORTH CORRECTING
# RATHER THAN DELETING, because it is the kind of wrong that reads as reassuring.
# It said `binary` is `-text -diff`, so "images there stay diffable as text".
# Measured with `git check-attr text diff merge`:
#
#   `binary`  →  text: unset        diff: unset        merge: unset
#   `-text`   →  text: unset        diff: unspecified  merge: unspecified
#
# So `binary` is the three-part macro `-text -diff -merge`, and the difference
# that matters is `-merge`: under the nested file's `-text`, git will attempt a
# textual three-way merge on a conflicting PNG or zip and write conflict markers
# into it. The claimed difference does not exist — measured, a NUL-bearing file
# (which is every real image) renders as "Binary files … differ" under `-text`
# exactly as it does under `binary`, because git's NUL sniffing decides that and
# no attribute overrides it. `-text` restores a readable diff only for a file with
# no NUL byte in it at all.
#
# This mattered because .githooks/pre-commit's content gate reads the rendered
# diff, so both markings used to blind it — the `binary` block below did so even
# for pure ASCII. That is fixed in the scanner, not here: the hook now passes
# `--text`, which overrides both the attribute and the NUL sniffing, and its
# self-test stages a token inside a `binary`-marked *.png and asserts the refusal.
# Fixing it here instead would have meant dropping `-merge` from every binary in
# the repository to make a grep work, which is the wrong file paying the cost.

# Normalise to LF in the repository AND on checkout, on every platform,
# regardless of the cloner's core.autocrlf setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

# PowerShell and cmd are the two formats that genuinely want CRLF on Windows.
*.ps1  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf

# Binaries: never line-ending-converted, never diffed as text.
# `text=auto` already infers this from NUL bytes; stating it removes the
# inference, so an archive whose first bytes happen to look textual cannot be
# misclassified and mangled.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.zip   binary
*.xpi   binary
*.crx   binary
*.webm  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary

# The session log is append-only and long, so it is collapsed by default rather
# than left to drown a pull request diff.
#
# ⚠️ THE PATTERN IS ANCHORED TO ONE PATH ON PURPOSE, AND THE BARE `HANDOFF.md` IT
# REPLACES WAS A CONTRADICTION, NOT A CONVENIENCE. A bare pattern matches
# HANDOFF.md at any depth, and every OTHER depth is a per-extension session log
# that .gitignore excludes from this repository entirely. So the old line said
# "still versioned, still reviewable" about the exact class of document the ignore
# file was written to withhold — two mechanisms committed the same day asserting
# opposite policies about the same filename. `linguist-generated=true` is a
# rendering hint for TRACKED files and is simply inert on an ignored one, so the
# contradiction cost nothing at runtime and misled every reader instead.
#
# templates/tool/HANDOFF.md is the one HANDOFF.md this repository does track: the
# skeleton's unfilled scaffold, deliberately public, carried by the matching
# negation in .gitignore. Naming it in full means this attribute now applies to
# exactly the file it describes, and a future HANDOFF.md that appears somewhere
# else gets no endorsement it should not have.
templates/tool/HANDOFF.md linguist-generated=true
